==English==
===Etymology===
The meaning "spell of nervousness," recorded since 1896, stems perhaps from the [[woollies]], a dialectal term for "nervous uneasiness," probably in reference to the physical [[itchiness]] of wool garments.
 
===Noun===
'''willies'''

# {{plural of|[[willy]]}}
# {{colloquial|with "the"}} A feeling of [[nervousness]] or fear (''usually in the phrase'' '''[[give someone the willies]]'''.)
#: I get the willies when I see closed doors. &mdash; Heller, ''Something Happened,'' 1974

